  "term": "delusion of negation",
  "definition": "A delusion of negation is a morbid belief, described in historical psychiatry, in which a person denies the reality or existence of themselves, parts of their body, or the world around them. In the passage, it is presented as a severe form of melancholic negative thinking that can progress from feeling changed or emptied to believing one is dead or that nothing exists.",
